1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
Meet OpenIDE. Your code, your AI agent,

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,000
and your running app, together in one workspace.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Choose a connected model,
then describe the change you want.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,000
OpenIDE brings the editor context
into the conversation.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Project Map connects files,
symbols, and dependencies.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Shared memory keeps the conventions
and decisions that matter,

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
so each session has a useful starting point.

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Review the plan, refine the details,
and decide what happens next.

9
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,000
The plan stays in your project,
ready to revisit.

10
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Watch the changes arrive in your editor.

11
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Inspect the diff, review affected files,
and keep the work you want.

12
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Then check the result
in the built-in browser.

13
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The agent can inspect the page
and capture what you see,

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
using the session already open.

15
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Prefer a coding CLI? Supported integrations

16
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
can use OpenIDE's browser, project context,

17
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
memory, and plan review,
while keeping their own workflow.

18
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Save the convention you learned,
and carry it into the next session.

19
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:28,000
OpenIDE. Explore the source,
and make it yours.
